[[[ Seed Differential Tests ]]]

Fixed message pairs (m, m'), uniformly random seeds; counting seeds with hash(m) == hash(m').
Base message has w1 == ~w0; ~wi means 64-bit word i of m is complemented in m'.
Ideal rate is 2^-64 per seed; a row fails above max(3, E + 6*sqrt(E)), E = seeds * 2^-64.

Default tier: 2^24 seeds per pair
